  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CB26310",
    "sub_id": "31508",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>課程評量方式將以下列比重評分， 尤其對於上課參與的部分，教師非常鼓勵學生培養獨立思考與邏輯能力， 並鼓勵學生於上課時能夠勇於發言討論。 出席率與上課參與40%， 指定閱讀報告30% , 個案期末專題研究報告30% 。</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "請各位同學務必準時於上課時間前到達教室，每個星期報告之同學請於上課前先將檔案下載於電腦桌面上。同學報告或老師講解時請勿聊天與玩手機，對於講台上報告之同學給予必須之尊重與同理心。請將手機關靜音，手機與電腦在上課期間僅限使用於相關之資料查詢與筆記。學期內請假僅限兩次，出席率將會影響各位的學習分數。",
    "course_pol_en": "【Classroom Rules】\n\nAll students are required to arrive at the classroom on time before the class begins.\n\nStudents scheduled to present each week must download and save their presentation files onto their computer desktops prior to class.\n\nDuring student presentations or the teacher's explanations, please refrain from chatting or using your mobile phone, and show the necessary respect and empathy toward the presenting students.\n\nPlease set your mobile phones to silent mode; during class, mobile phones and computers should only be used for accessing relevant information and taking notes.\n\nEach student is allowed a maximum of two absences per semester, and attendance will affect your overall academic performance.",
    "course_rem": "上課發問發言對我來說是很重要的學習方式之一，所以我也希望大家可以踴躍的發言發問，沒有笨問題，只有不敢發問的笨小孩。\n如果對於任何學習上的不理解，請大家隨時於上課時舉手提出，或是下課時間與我討論。",
    "course_rem_en": "【Class Reminder】\nActive participation and asking questions in class are essential learning methods, so I encourage everyone to engage actively. Remember, there are no stupid questions—only students who are hesitant to ask them. If you have any questions about the course content, please feel free to raise your hand during class or discuss with me after class.",
    "ais_meno": "<div>\n<ul>\n\t<li>學術誠信提醒<br />\n\t學術誠信敬請學生遵守。依據國際學術誠信中心（International Center for Academic Integrity，2021）所提出的六項學術誠信核心價值，包括：誠實、信任、公平、尊重、責任與勇氣，學生應在高等教育課堂中實踐這些原則。</li>\n\t<li>參考資料<br />\n\t潘璿安（2021）。<em>給大學生的參考手冊──在高等教育課堂中實踐學術誠信</em>〔電子書〕。教育部臺灣學術倫理教育資源中心。檢自 https://ethics.moe.edu.tw/files/resource/ebook/file/ebook_02_cn.pdf（取用日期：2023年9月1日）。</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Academic Integrity Reminder</div>\n\n<div>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Students are expected to uphold academic integrity. According to the International Center for Academic Integrity (2021), the six fundamental values of academic integrity are honesty, trust, fairness, respect, responsibility, and courage. These principles should be practiced in all higher education classrooms.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div>Reference:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Pan, Hsuan-An. (2021). <em>A Guidebook for University Students: Practicing Academic Integrity in Higher Education Classrooms</em> [E-book]. Taiwan Academic Ethics Education Resource Center, Ministry of Education. Retrieved from <a href=\"https://ethics.moe.edu.tw/files/resource/ebook/file/ebook_02_cn.pdf\" target=\"_new\">https://ethics.moe.edu.tw/files/resource/ebook/file/ebook_02_cn.pdf</a> (Accessed: September 1, 2023).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
